      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n- Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to **6,400 mg/day**. That is twice the usual maximum for a hospitalized adult of 3,200 mg/day.\n- A single 1600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg.\n- At this level the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up substantially, even when kidney and liver function are normal.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day total)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), which is a common anti-inflammatory dose\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that it's intentional and give the clinical rationale for the order note. I'd still suggest checking it with pharmacy or your attending first."
      }
     ],
